        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: New York Stakes, Belmont Stakes\n- Places: Belmont Park, Elmont, New York, Long Island, New York City\n- Concepts: American Thoroughbred horse racing\n- People: Avatar\n\nFacts:\n- Belmont Park first opened on May 4, 1905.\n- Avatar was an American Thoroughbred racehorse born on March 10, 1972, and he won the 1975 Belmont Stakes.\n- Avatar died on December 3, 1992.\n- The New York Stakes is an American Thoroughbred horse race held annually at Belmont Park in Elmont, Long Island, New York.\n- The Belmont Stakes is an American Grade I stakes Thoroughbred horse race held every June at Belmont Park in Elmont, New York.\n- Belmont Park is a major Thoroughbred horse-racing facility in Elmont, New York, just outside New York City limits.\n- The New York Stakes purse was increased to $500,000 for 2016.",
